{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/904-ethan-skemp-s-clarification-on-oneiromancy","id":904,"title":"Ethan Skemp's Clarification on Oneiromancy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T21:49:50-07:00","id":904,"title":"Ethan Skemp's Clarification on Oneiromancy","content":"<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">This comes from a rather old thread that Ethan responded to but I've referred to it more than once over the years and thought it would help if it survived the journey to the new forums. I haven't added to it or taken anything away; I've just tried to format it a little to make it easy to read.<br /> <br /> Clarification on Oneiromancy</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Quote:</b><br /> Can a changeling enter any dream? Or is dreamriding limited to the changeling's fetch &amp; those he has dream task pledges with?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Through basic oneiromancery, you're limited to you, your fetch, or those with dreaming task pledges. Forging the Dream can be used on anyone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Quote:</b><br /> When is a roll required for entering a dream? </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When you can't see your target. No roll is necessary when you can see them as they sleep.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Quote:</b><br /> When does a changeling have to be in the Hedge to enter a dream?</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">When you're searching for the dreams of someone that you can't perceive; essentially, when you need to reach someone in an unknown location.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Quote:</b> What does the difficulty table at the beginning of oneiromancy mean?<br /> Are these difficulties for entering different classes of dreams? If so, can you clarify what these classes mean? </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">That's essentially a measure for how long it takes to enter a dream. The &quot;personal dreams&quot; should be omitted from that table; it takes no time for a changeling to enter their own dreams. The average time to enter a fetch's dreams might, assuming two successes per roll, require three hours of meditation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Quote:</b><br /> Finally, how does the Forging the Dream clause work? Is this simply a way to project a dream to someone, another method of entering someone's dreams, or a form of dreamriding? If it is simply a means of dream projection, I assume it is only limited to basic memory, wish-fufillment, or nightmare type dreams (a changeling could not create special effect dreams like dreamshaping).</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">It's essentially dreamscaping; the Contract is basically a form of specialization in oneiromancy that allows for less fuss and less time invested.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","user":"KismetRose","date":". 11-02-2013, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:29:02-08:00","id":5366,"title":"","content":"Was anything ever discussed with all of this + the Material from Dancers in the Dusk? Skeinwalking in particular specifies that it eliminates the restriction of self/pledge/fetch from Oneiromancy, but there still seems to be &quot;missing&quot; functions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img835/1264/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Do you see over yonder, friend Sancho, thirty or forty hulking giants? I intend to do battle with them and slay them.&quot;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/441-nighttrace","name":"NightTrace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar441_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:41:50-08:00","id":5375,"title":"","content":"I believe this was well before Dancers in the Dusk was released. Maybe we can get Ethan in here sometime for those questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:27:07-08:00","id":5475,"title":"","content":"I noticed you missed the second part of the Q&amp;A:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quote:</b><br /> Huh, interesting. All this time I had thought that you absolutely had to be in the Hedge to enter non-fetch dreams unless you had Dream 2. </div> </div> </div>That's the literal reading, though I think I prefer opening it up a bit more as above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quote:</b><br /> Alright, so, if Dream 2 allows you to do anything that dreamscaping can do (including Healing Sleep, Sleep Teaching, ect.), am I correct in assuming that the clause also allows you to perform lower functions of dream-shaping, such as dream riding? </div> </div> </div>Essentially.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quote:</b><br /> What about oneiromachy? </div> </div> </div>The clause refers directly to oneiromachy, so I would assume so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quote:</b><br /> Also, what is the Intensity of a dream created with Forging the Dream? </div> </div> </div>Resolved as usual, though I would think it appropriate to have it be determined instead by the Wits + Wyrd roll made to activate the clause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quote:</b><br /> So if you're in the presence of a sleeper do you still need to fall asleep yourself? Or can you do it while awake? </div> </div> </div>You should fall asleep yourself. The &quot;when you can see them as they sleep&quot; should be just before you start activating the power, hence nodding off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Quote:</b><br /> So am I right in concluding that Forging the Dream allows you to manipulate someone's dream, but not to see what their original dreams are? </div> </div> </div>You are correct. It's a powerful but specialized ability.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 11-07-2013, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T20:26:52-08:00","id":5703,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Penta; I knew something was missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}